   "source": [
    "# Systematic Sampling\n",
    "\n",
    "In systematic sampling we select every n-th element.\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "Population = 1000\n",
    "Sample size = 100\n",
    "\n",
    "k = 1000 / 100 = 10\n",
    "\n",
    "So we pick:\n",
    "\n",
    "10th, 20th, 30th, 40th person etc."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "d3efe24b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[ 1 11 21 31 41 51 61 71 81 91]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "population = np.arange(1,101)\n",
    "\n",
    "sample = population[::10]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(sample)"
   ]
  }
 ],
